  if (t === 'GROUP_UNRESOLVABLE') return false; // v64: permanent — page fetched, no id in HTML; a 30-min retry can't help (a transient resolve failure is tagged EXCEPTION and still retries)
  // ── 🔴 a DOM/Safe post that MIGHT have landed is never retried ────────────
  // The Safe path drives Facebook's composer; it carries NO idempotence token,
  // so a retry is a genuine SECOND post into someone's group. The failover path
  // has always understood this (classifyDomFailover → 'maybe-landed' → no
  // failover) — the RETRY QUEUE did not, and `timeout` matches its
  // "transient" regex, so an uncertain Safe post was re-sent 60 seconds later.
  //
  // Listed explicitly rather than derived: classifyDomFailover treats every
  // unknown string as maybe-landed, and 'UNKNOWN' from the Fast path SHOULD
  // still retry (it is idempotence-protected). Only these are DOM outcomes
  // whose fate we cannot know.
